# Round XXVIII Track C POS fixture — a function CALL ARG `!x` (parser pre-
# strips the `!` into `CallArg.ownership = Move`, so it never reaches the
# EMove chokepoint) is a RESTING / consuming-boundary position; must ACCEPT
# and run. This is the closest single-fixture we can ship for the "spawn/
# await value" and "capture-list" ALLOW-list cells: the mechanism is the
# same parser-pre-strip through `parse_ownership_modifier`
# (`src/parser/mod.rs:267`). Spawn end-to-end tests exist elsewhere and are
# gated by C-backend spawn work.

int consume(String !name):
    print(!name)
    return 0

void main():
    String s = "hello"
    int _r = consume(!s)
